"Universal Music"},{"animation":false,"id":6616,"name":"BS11"},{"animation":false,"id":238,"name":"AT-X"},{"animation":false,"id":460,"name":"KLOCKWORX"},{"animation":false,"id":382,"name":"Tokuma Shoten"}],"synopsis":{"language":null,"source":"anilist","spoiler":false,"text":"Picture book author Hotaru Yuuyami lost his beloved dog, Hanako. He was in the depths of a dark and deep sadness, regretting his inability to do anything about it. One day, he notices a pink mushroom growing under the snow willow tree in his garden. As he gazed at it idly, it suddenly began to move, wagging its tail and coming closer to him. “A mushroom...dog?”\n\nDespite his doubts, he decides to live with this mysterious creature, “Kinokoinu\" (Mushroom Dog). Then he started drawing where he wasn't supposed to draw, ate all the melon bread and takoyaki, and made all sorts of messes, but his playful attitude is hard to hate.\n\nThe days spent with Kinokoinu, involving his childhood friend Komako-chan, the editor, and Yara-kun of the Mushroom Research Institute, gradually changes Hotaru's expression. This is a slightly mysterious and heartwarming animation that depicts the funny days of Hotaru and everyone together with Kinokoinu, who is too mysterious in many ways.\n\n(Source: Crunchyroll News, edited)"},"tags":[{"name":"Iyashikei","rank":85,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Adult Cast","rank":80,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Rehabilitation","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Drawing","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Writing","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Anthropomorphism","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Orphan","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Work","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Animals","rank":75,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Seinen","rank":75,"spoiler":false},{"name":"LGBTQ+ Themes","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Bisexual","rank":50,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Boys' Love","rank":40,"spoiler":true}],"titles":{"display